-- title:
--   Fricke involution at level 1· p sends j to j(qᵖ)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime. The level is written in the unreduced form $1 \cdot p$ throughout. The ambient field is `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull (1 * p)`, the intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the divisor expansions at that level; `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * p)` is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism of this base change obtained, via `geomAut`, by transporting along the base-change isomorphism the $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphism `frickeInvolutionFull (1 * p)`, which is a chosen automorphism satisfying the predicate `IsFrickeAutFull (1 * p)` if one exists and the identity otherwise. The two elements compared are `jF p`, the image of the Laurent series `jq` under the coefficientwise map `coeffEmb` induced by $\mathbb Q \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$, and `jpF p`, the image under `coeffEmb` of `qExpand ℚ p jq`, the substitution $q \mapsto q^{p}$ realised by multiplying the exponent support by $p$. The assertion is the equality $\mathrm{frickeInvolutionBar}(1 \cdot p)\,(j) = j(q^{p})$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`.
--
--   This is the classical Atkin–Lehner relation $w_p\, j = j(q^p)$ on the function field of $X_0(p)$, recorded in the spelling (level index $1 \cdot p$, elements `jF` and `jpF`) used by the multiplicative-covering charts, so that statements about the second chart of $X_0(p)$ can be read as transports of the first along the Fricke involution. It is used in the construction of lifts of $j$ near the singular point of the covering, through [`ModularCurve.MultCovering.exists_lift_jF_sub_mem_chart_src_integers_and_ord_nodeSrc_pos`](thm.html#ModularCurve.MultCovering.exists_lift_jF_sub_mem_chart_src_integers_and_ord_nodeSrc_pos).
